    "0.1.3": {
      "bundle": {
        "sha256": "7606e8ba20209c9c9458f66acc018c3dc63de4135344553e0cdbe256bea360f5",
        "size": 11395,
        "url": "https://github.com/lapismd/lapis-plugins/releases/download/source-editor%400.1.3/lapis-source-editor-0.1.3.lapis-plugin",
      },
      "changelog": {
        "description": "### Patch Changes\n\n- [#28](https://github.com/lapismd/lapis-plugins/pull/28) [`d27467e`](https://github.com/lapismd/lapis-plugins/commit/d27467ee80c273011b7eb6ae792fa8e0330a11c1) Thanks [@stevejuma](https://github.com/stevejuma)! - Align shared presentation dependencies with the Design Core 0.6 public boundary used by current Notes hosts.\n\n- [#28](https://github.com/lapismd/lapis-plugins/pull/28) [`f4b9136`](https://github.com/lapismd/lapis-plugins/commit/f4b9136e4f47965700e06f52f82e8e2bc884eb11) Thanks [@stevejuma](https://github.com/stevejuma)! - Accept Design Core 0.5.1 alongside the existing 0.4 release line so current local\n  Desktop builds can use one compatible framework graph.\n\n- [#28](https://github.com/lapismd/lapis-plugins/pull/28) [`56b5d6c`](https://github.com/lapismd/lapis-plugins/commit/56b5d6c1a016ef9bca43703b5fecf57f8234d1af) Thanks [@stevejuma](https://github.com/stevejuma)! - Consume published Design Core 0.4.0 with prepared browser CSS and bundled font assets through normal npm ranges.\n\n  Restore Bases picker input/list accessibility relationships and name property actions.\n\n- [#28](https://github.com/lapismd/lapis-plugins/pull/28) [`c9febb1`](https://github.com/lapismd/lapis-plugins/commit/c9febb1c8b431db30ecdcf7507cfff8f727bc4ed) Thanks [@stevejuma](https://github.com/stevejuma)! - Consume the published Notes next packages, Mira 0.1.2, and Design Core 0.7.0 through the existing semver floors. Markdown dependents accept ^0.2.0. History keeps its public repository entrypoints, and Bases keeps the file-icon contract on API 0.2.0.",
        "title": "Source Editor 0.1.3",
      },
      "minAppVersion": "0.1.0",
      "platforms": ["web", "desktop"],
      "releasedAt": "2026-10-30T15:58:18.000Z",
      "version": "0.1.3",
    },
  },
